<!--
Landscape: now playing beside the launcher grid rather than above it.

Stacked, the two do not both fit.  A landscape phone is about 300dp tall and
the grid alone wants two thirds of that, which left the title clipped, the
scrub bar half drawn, and the play controls entirely below the fold.  Side by
side, each column needs about the height it already had in portrait, and there
is width to spare: the detail column's own content is no wider than the 220dp
play controls, and three buttons across half a landscape screen are still
wider than three across a portrait one.

Even halves.  The detail side is the screen's subject and holds the widest
fixed item, so it should not be the narrower of the two.
-->
<LinearLayout xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
  android:orientation="horizontal"
  android:baselineAligned="false"
  android:layout_width="match_parent"
  android:layout_height="match_parent"
  android:layout_margin="8dp"
  android:fitsSystemWindows="true"
>
  <ScrollView android:layout_weight="1" android:fillViewport="true"
    android:layout_width="0dp" android:layout_height="match_parent"
  >
    <include layout="@layout/now_showing_detail" />
  </ScrollView>

  <include layout="@layout/now_showing_nav"
    android:layout_width="0dp" android:layout_height="match_parent"
    android:layout_weight="1" android:layout_marginStart="8dp" />
</LinearLayout>
